            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">The area between your shoulder blades is what we call the "trouble triangle" — it's the hardest zone to reach and the most commonly missed. The secret: <strong>extend the handle fully, reach over the opposite shoulder, and use slow diagonal strokes</strong>. Switch arms halfway through. A back shaver with a pivoting head makes this zone dramatically easier.</p>
