          </p>

          <div class="bg-[#1E90FF]/5 border-l-4 border-[#1E90FF] p-6 my-8 rounded-r-2xl">
            <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 m-0 mb-2">Does Hair Grow Back Faster If You Shave?</p>
            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">No. Shaving has zero effect on the speed of hair regrowth. Back hair grows at approximately <strong>1/4 to 1/2 inch per month</strong> regardless of whether you shave, wax, or leave it alone. The growth rate is controlled by your hair follicles, which sit deep beneath the skin — far below where a razor blade can reach.</p>
